'' ARRAY RESULTS: 'function foo( ) as integer( )' returns a dynamic array -- a tiko extension
'' (fbc's error 3). The result travels through the hidden pointer, the caller owns it, and
'' 'return' takes a brace list, a local array (moved) or a call that returns one. See
'' symbols/arrresult.bas and mir/lowerarrret.bas.
''
'' RUN, because a lost move or a missing erase compiles, verifies and prints the right numbers
'' before it faults -- the thousand-iteration loop at the end is what shows a double free.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/array-result.bas -o tests/driver/arrayresult.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/arrayresult.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/arrayresult.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: var 10 20 30 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: local 0 16 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: result 7 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: replaced 4 5 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: string alpha gamma 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ustring x yy
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: empty -1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: relay 10 30
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: double 0.5 1.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: pick -1 11 12
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: take 0 2 30
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: show 0 2 20
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: each 60
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: assign 7 8 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: statement ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: loop 34000
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: udt 3 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 5 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: counts 2 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: strudt onetwo2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: nested 0 2 20 60
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: nestedeach 120
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: show 0 2 40
